A||||7||Zman302||E-brake||||5||
Z||000000||Zman302||06-16-2000||01:05 AM||||My car is up for inspection at the end of this month and my E-brake has not worked since i got the car.  Got my new cables and found i could not install them because most of the parts were missing.  Got the parts from the junk yard today and going to do the work this weekend.  What i would like to know is if anyone has any tricks to hooking these things up.  I will be replacing everything except the front cable that is still good.  Any suggestions or links to help me out would be greatly appreciated. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||My7Fieros||06-16-2000||03:21 AM||||I know this may be a stupid reply, but do you know if the car has ever been taken back for this prob? What I mean is, there was a recall years ago on all Fieros about the ebrake..there should be a sticker under the decklid...i cant remember the recall "code" on the sticker though...if not, take it to Pontiac, after they b*tch and moan for having to work on a Fiero, they'll fix it...FOR FREE!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||06-16-2000||09:36 AM||||The only tip I could offer is to cut some heater hose and wrap it around the cables where they pass through the cradle and spaceframe to prevent friction from eventually wearing through the sheath and causing the cable to rust.  This is what caused my front cable to die prematurely - Pontiac put a plastic shield around every hole, but two were broken.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Majik||06-16-2000||08:09 PM||||Have you checked to see if your car has been in for the recal on the braking system?  <BR>I know that the recal states that the e-brake system is prone to failing.<P>Check GM Campaign 86-C-16.  Hope this helps.  The campaign has been done on my 86GT and the e-brake holds like superglue.<P>Hope this helps||||reg||1
Z||000004||MikeE||06-17-2000||08:34 AM||||This topic was discussed on 6-1-00 under the heading "E-brake" so you might want to take a look at that.<P>According to a response from 2birds, the recall info is:<P>Recall # 86-C-16||||reg||1
Z||000005||Zman302||06-18-2000||12:58 AM||||Thanks for the replys.  ended up replacing all three cables.  One good thing was the calipers were still good and brakes work fine.  About the recall, it didnt cover my car because it is a automatic.  Job went alot better than i suspected.  I've done alot of e-brake cables on older cars with drums but never rear disc.  took about two hours total for all the cables and changing pads and greasing the sliders which were stuck.  Thanks again||||reg||1
Z||000006||2birds||06-18-2000||01:04 AM||||Sorry, forgot it only applied to manuals.  Some F-bodies were also covered, too.<P>Aren't the calipers the same for manuals and automatics?  What gives with the exclusion of the slushboxes??||||reg||1
Z||000007||Zman302||06-18-2000||01:31 AM||||Yeah they are identical.  I read somewhere on the net that GM somehow got around it.  Something like with a stick car you can work on the car running without setting the brake but on the autos you have park.  What sucks is i have never found the need to use it but this state requires it for the state inspection.||||reg||1
